  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing App Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the codebase structure, specifically the suggested directory layout for the application. The goal is to ensure a logical organization, focusing on clear separation of concerns, such as the UI components: home, apps, connections, privacy, and settings. I want to make sure it\'s intuitive and scales well.\n\n\n**Defining Database Structure**\n\nI\'ve been working on the database layer and have started to flesh out the schema. Specifically, I am focusing on the `AppRuleEntity.kt` data class. I am defining its attributes and their initial properties, including a primary key, to capture crucial data such as the package name, application name, UID, and various blocking preferences for network types and states. I am going to have it block all network traffic by default.\n\n\n**Expanding Database Schemas**\n\nI\'m now focusing on expanding the database schemas with additional entities and their attributes. I\'m introducing `ConnectionLogEntity.kt` to track network connections, noting the destination host, protocol, blocking status, and reasons. I\'m also adding `BlocklistEntity.kt` to manage blocked domains, including categories for easy filtering. I\'m also defining a `FirewallDao.kt` for the database access layer.\n\n\n**Defining Database Access**\n\nI\'m now in the process of defining the data access layer using a `FirewallDao`. This includes adding methods for inserting, deleting, and clearing rules, as well as logging and retrieving connection data. Specifically, I\'m integrating methods for getting recent and blocked logs, and inserting connection entries, while adding methods to get daily blocked and allowed counts, and top blocked apps. I\'m also adding methods for blocklist management, including insertion, deletion, and toggling of items, and clearing of categories within the blocklist. Additionally, I plan on using a Room database and prepopulating with known ad, tracker, and malware domains on the first creation.\n\n\n**Implementing Packet Handling**\n\nI\'m now integrating the packet parsing and rule engine within the VPN service. I\'ve designed `PacketParser.kt` as a lightweight tool to dissect DNS queries over UDP, focusing on extracting the queried domain names, like `graph.facebook.com`. This will allow me to create synthetic DNS responses, such as NXDOMAIN, or `0.0.0.0`. I\'m also building `RuleEngine.kt`, which determines if connections are allowed or blocked by cross-referencing against various configurations.\n\n\n**Orchestrating VPN Setup**\n\nI\'m currently finalizing the VPN setup, including screen and network change receivers. I\'m focusing on the virtual interface and addressing, using `10.1.10.1` and `fd00::1`. I\'m configuring allowed and disallowed application rules. I\'m also ensuring the packet-handling pipeline is correctly processing the `FileInputStream` data. The packets are read from `FileInputStream`, which are parsed for IP data. DNS is detected and checked against the RuleEngine blocklists, so they are either answered locally with a sinkhole or forwarded.\n\n\n\n**Refining VPN Logic**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the logic for permitted applications to ensure minimal latency. I am excluding permitted apps via `addDisallowedApplication(packageName)`, so that these apps experience zero latency. I am also working on clean shutdown, teardown, and notification dismissal procedures. This also encompasses designing methods to listen for tile clicks from Android\'s Quick Settings drawer, to toggle Firewall ON/OFF directly from the system shade!\n\n\n**Integrating App Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating the app management layer. I\'m using `PackageManager` to load installed apps, extracting key details. This covers names, package names, UID, version, icons (safely converted to `ImageBitmap` for display), whether they\'re system apps, and their permissions, like internet access. I am also synchronizing the app data with the Room database, ensuring all apps with internet permissions have an entry in `AppRuleEntity`. I have also added features to search and filter apps within the UI.\n\n\n**Designing App Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now designing the app\'s main dashboard. I\'m focusing on a clean, high-contrast, light theme. I\'m planning a bottom navigation bar with five destinations: Dashboard, Apps, Connections, Privacy, and Settings. The dashboard will have an animated status card, status tiles, and quick controls for firewall actions and modes. I\'m also including a live connection feed.\n\n\n\n**Designing App Screens**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Apps screen with a search field and filter chips for easy app management. Batch actions like \"Block All Non-System\" are included. The app card itself will have quick toggle buttons and open an AppDetailBottomSheet. This sheet offers advanced toggles and network rule selectors with clear Android system constraint explanations.\n\nI am also working on the Connections screen, which will include a live feed of connection attempts from the Room database. I am including filter tabs, a search bar, a summary header with key stats, and export/clear log buttons.\n\n\n**Crafting Privacy Screen**\n\nI\'m now building the Privacy Screen. It will include a DNS-based filtering master toggle and curated protection categories, such as ad, tracker, and malware blocking. I\'m also implementing a custom blocklist manager, where I can add, disable, and delete custom domains. I am going to have an honest notice explaining how the filtering works locally on the device, to ensure privacy.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 722412996
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
