  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Firewall Service**\n\nI\'m now focusing on creating `firewall/FirewallVpnService.kt`. I\'m going to carefully build the core service. It will inherit from `VpnService` and manage a notification channel named `netguardian_firewall_channel`. This includes a persistent notification with M3 styling and PendingIntents for stopping the service and launching the MainActivity. I\'ll also register a dynamic Screen BroadcastReceiver.\n\n\n**Implementing Screen Handling**\n\nI\'ve got the screen state handling pretty nailed down now. I\'m using `Intent.ACTION_SCREEN_ON` to signal `firewallManager.setScreenState(true)` and `Intent.ACTION_SCREEN_OFF` to signal `firewallManager.setScreenState(false)`. This is essential because it triggers a rule re-evaluation. I\'m focusing next on core VPN establishment and packet filtering.\n\n\n**Analyzing Packet Filtering**\n\nI\'m deep in the weeds of packet handling now, focusing on non-root blocking. Permitted apps can bypass the VPN entirely for speed, or, if DNS filtering is active, get inspected locally. I\'m reading packets from a `ParcelFileDescriptor` to identify DNS queries (UDP port 53). I\'m parsing domain names, cross-checking against blocklists, and sending back a sinkhole response to instantly block trackers if needed, and logging the connections.\n\n\n"
