    thinking: "**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing the UI components. Specifically, I\'m thinking about the `DashboardScreen.kt`, and have conceptualized a VPN Status Card. This card will feature an animated radar ring, an ON/OFF indicator, and prominent \"Start Firewall\" / \"Stop Firewall\" buttons, for easy user interaction.\n\n\n**Expanding App Control Features**\n\nI\'ve moved on from the VPN status and am now fleshing out the `AppsScreen.kt` UI. I\'ve designed the tiles for stats, quick controls, and a new battery and data transparency card. I\'ve also added a live connection preview card. Further, I\'ve incorporated search functionality and filter chips. I\'m focusing on the `AppCard`, implementing quick toggle buttons, and considering the full rules configuration within an `AppDetailDialog`.\n\n\n**Developing Privacy Features**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the privacy aspect, focusing on the `PrivacyScreen.kt` UI. I\'ve got a Master DNS Filtering switch in place, and am working on curated categories for Ad Blocking, Tracker Blocking, and Malware/Phishing Domain Protection. Each will have a switch and a counter. I\'m also adding a Custom Blocklist section with a text field and an \"Add\" button for custom domains, and I am adding a note about Android\'s VPN restrictions.\n\n\n\n**Expanding Settings Menu**\n\nI\'m now expanding the settings menu, particularly focusing on the SettingsScreen.kt UI. I\'m adding firewall settings like \"start on boot\" and persistent notifications. I\'m also including a default rule for new apps. I\'m building a background activity control section that will provide a detailed explanation of Android\'s power management and battery killers. I\'m also adding theme options and backup/restore functionality and a reset to factory default. Finally, I\'m composing an \"About NetGuardian\" section that will provide technical disclosures.\n\n\n"
