    response: "I have completed the implementation of **NetGuardian**, a privacy-focused per-app network firewall and background activity controller for Android.\n\n### Architectural & Functional Highlights\n\n- **VpnService Filtering Engine**:\n  - Implemented an on-device packet filtering engine utilizing Android\'s `VpnService` loopback interface for non-root traffic restriction.\n  - Granularly routes and isolates traffic on a per-application basis using Linux UIDs and package names.\n  - Dynamically responds to network switches (Wi-Fi vs. Cellular) and screen state transitions (`ACTION_SCREEN_ON` / `ACTION_SCREEN_OFF`) to enforce policies in real time.\n\n- **Dashboard**:\n  - Displays real-time firewall status with animated radar pulse indicators and a prominent toggle control.\n  - Surfaces four dynamic status tiles: Blocked Applications, Allowed Applications, Daily Block Events, and Active Network Interface (Wi-Fi, Cellular, or Offline).\n  - Integrates one-tap quick modes: **Normal**, **Block Non-System**, **Wi-Fi Only**, and **Mobile Data Only**.\n  - Features an activity preview card linking directly to full connection inspection logs.\n\n- **Installed Apps Manager & Granular Rules**:\n  - Dynamically queries installed packages, loads cached application icons, and badges system versus user apps alongside system UIDs.\n  - Enables instant one-tap toggles for total blocking, Wi-Fi restriction, and mobile data restriction directly on each app card.\n  - Includes a detailed configuration sheet for fine-grained control:\n    - Wi-Fi network access\n    - Cellular data access\n    - Background data restriction\n    - Block when screen is off\n    - Tracker and ad domain blocking\n  - Provides batch actions to block all non-system applications or reset all apps to allowed.\n\n- **Live Connection Log**:\n  - Records real-time outbound connection attempts into a local Room database with zero cloud telemetry.\n  - Displays destination host, port number, protocol (TCP, UDP, DNS), blocked/allowed status chip, filter reason, and timestamps.\n  - Offers filtering by event status (All, Blocked, Allowed) and text search by domain, IP, or application name.\n\n- **DNS Sinkhole & Privacy Protection**:\n  - Built-in UDP port 53 DNS packet parser and synthetic response synthesizer returning `0.0.0.0` sinkhole answers to block tracker queries without timeout delays.\n  - Pre-populated curated local blocklists for Advertising, Tracking & Telemetry, and Malware/Phishing domains.\n  - Custom blocklist manager allowing users to add, toggle, or delete specific domains.\n\n- **Settings & Android System Transparency**:\n  - Technically honest deep-dive explaining Android platform constraints: the distinction between network restriction versus process termination, Doze mode, App Standby Buckets, and OEM task management.\n  - Direct shortcut to system Battery Optimization Whitelist settings to ensure continuous protection.\n  - Automation toggles for start-on-boot and persistent notification shade status.\n  - Complete JSON-based export and import functionality for firewall configurations, plus a full reset-to-defaults option.\n  - Quick Settings Tile integration (`FirewallTileService`) for status toggling directly from the Android quick settings shade."
    modified_response: "I have completed the implementation of **NetGuardian**, a privacy-focused per-app network firewall and background activity controller for Android.\n\n### Architectural & Functional Highlights\n\n- **VpnService Filtering Engine**:\n  - Implemented an on-device packet filtering engine utilizing Android\'s `VpnService` loopback interface for non-root traffic restriction.\n  - Granularly routes and isolates traffic on a per-application basis using Linux UIDs and package names.\n  - Dynamically responds to network switches (Wi-Fi vs. Cellular) and screen state transitions (`ACTION_SCREEN_ON` / `ACTION_SCREEN_OFF`) to enforce policies in real time.\n\n- **Dashboard**:\n  - Displays real-time firewall status with animated radar pulse indicators and a prominent toggle control.\n  - Surfaces four dynamic status tiles: Blocked Applications, Allowed Applications, Daily Block Events, and Active Network Interface (Wi-Fi, Cellular, or Offline).\n  - Integrates one-tap quick modes: **Normal**, **Block Non-System**, **Wi-Fi Only**, and **Mobile Data Only**.\n  - Features an activity preview card linking directly to full connection inspection logs.\n\n- **Installed Apps Manager & Granular Rules**:\n  - Dynamically queries installed packages, loads cached application icons, and badges system versus user apps alongside system UIDs.\n  - Enables instant one-tap toggles for total blocking, Wi-Fi restriction, and mobile data restriction directly on each app card.\n  - Includes a detailed configuration sheet for fine-grained control:\n    - Wi-Fi network access\n    - Cellular data access\n    - Background data restriction\n    - Block when screen is off\n    - Tracker and ad domain blocking\n  - Provides batch actions to block all non-system applications or reset all apps to allowed.\n\n- **Live Connection Log**:\n  - Records real-time outbound connection attempts into a local Room database with zero cloud telemetry.\n  - Displays destination host, port number, protocol (TCP, UDP, DNS), blocked/allowed status chip, filter reason, and timestamps.\n  - Offers filtering by event status (All, Blocked, Allowed) and text search by domain, IP, or application name.\n\n- **DNS Sinkhole & Privacy Protection**:\n  - Built-in UDP port 53 DNS packet parser and synthetic response synthesizer returning `0.0.0.0` sinkhole answers to block tracker queries without timeout delays.\n  - Pre-populated curated local blocklists for Advertising, Tracking & Telemetry, and Malware/Phishing domains.\n  - Custom blocklist manager allowing users to add, toggle, or delete specific domains.\n\n- **Settings & Android System Transparency**:\n  - Technically honest deep-dive explaining Android platform constraints: the distinction between network restriction versus process termination, Doze mode, App Standby Buckets, and OEM task management.\n  - Direct shortcut to system Battery Optimization Whitelist settings to ensure continuous protection.\n  - Automation toggles for start-on-boot and persistent notification shade status.\n  - Complete JSON-based export and import functionality for firewall configurations, plus a full reset-to-defaults option.\n  - Quick Settings Tile integration (`FirewallTileService`) for status toggling directly from the Android quick settings shade."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
