 such as the text color, background color, and overall visual appearance. I\'m particularly interested in class names like `text-sm`, `font-bold`, `bg-[#D1E4FF]`, `px-2`, and `py-0.5` which are key indicators of design choices and layout patterns, I will be referencing these for modification.\n\n\n**Defining the Palette**\n\nOkay, I\'m now documenting and categorizing the color palette meticulously. I\'ve noted primary and secondary text colors, backgrounds for various states, error and success colors, along with supporting variants. The goal is to create a consistent design language. I\'m focusing on the hex codes provided to establish a design standard.\n\n\n"
