    modified_response: "I have applied the **Sleek Interface** design aesthetic throughout **NetGuardian**, preserving all functionality, components, and structure while updating typography, color palettes, card treatments, and interactive states:\n\n- **Sleek Palette & Tokens**: Established a clean palette based on the design specification with a light canvas (`#FDFBFF`), crisp card surfaces (`#FFFFFF`), subtle borders (`#C2C7CF`), deep blue primary accents (`#0061A4`), soft containers (`#D1E4FF`), and restrained semantic alert indicators (`#BA1A1A` for blocked, `#0061A4` for allowed/safe).\n- **Top Header & Bottom Navigation**: Refined the application top bar with status pills and modernized the navigation bar with active container highlights, pill badges, and refined typography.\n- **Dashboard Screen**: Styled the primary hero status card, real-time metrics grid, quick mode buttons, and transparency cards with rounded card geometry, subtle borders, and balanced negative space.\n- **Installed Apps Screen**: Updated the search field, filter chips, batch action toggles, per-app cards, and the rule configuration bottom sheet.\n- **Connection Logs Screen**: Polished search, live rate summary bar, log item cards, and confirmation dialogs with crisp type pairings and clear visual hierarchy.\n- **Privacy & Settings Screens**: Styled DNS toggle controls, category protection cards, custom domain management, and configuration export/import dialogs to match the Sleek theme."
