steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1788464870
      nanos: 394518198
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "Create a dedicated \'Background Activity\' section in NetGuardian. For each application, allow users to toggle options such as \'Allow background network,\' \'Block background network,\' \'Block when screen is off,\' and \'Block when device is idle.\' Clearly explain Android\'s limitations regarding background execution control based on version and manufacturer.\n\nImplement optional DNS-based filtering for NetGuardian. Allow users to enable ad blocking, tracker blocking, and malware-domain blocking. Provide a simple rule management screen for custom blocklists. Ensure no third-party server is hardcoded as mandatory and the feature works locally.\n\nImplement quick controls for NetGuardian. Include toggles for \'Firewall ON/OFF,\' \'Block all non-system apps,\' \'Allow all apps,\' \'Wi-Fi-only mode,\' and \'Mobile-data-only mode.\' These controls should be accessible via an persistent notification and a Quick Settings tile where supported by Android."
    items {
      text: "Create a dedicated \'Background Activity\' section in NetGuardian. For each application, allow users to toggle options such as \'Allow background network,\' \'Block background network,\' \'Block when screen is off,\' and \'Block when device is idle.\' Clearly explain Android\'s limitations regarding background execution control based on version and manufacturer.\n\nImplement optional DNS-based filtering for NetGuardian. Allow users to enable ad blocking, tracker blocking, and malware-domain blocking. Provide a simple rule management screen for custom blocklists. Ensure no third-party server is hardcoded as mandatory and the feature works locally.\n\nImplement quick controls for NetGuardian. Include toggles for \'Firewall ON/OFF,\' \'Block all non-system apps,\' \'Allow all apps,\' \'Wi-Fi-only mode,\' and \'Mobile-data-only mode.\' These controls should be accessible via an persistent notification and a Quick Settings tile where supported by Android."
    }
  }
}
