  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Local DNS Sinkholing**\n\nI\'m making good progress! I\'ve confirmed the DNS sinkholing in `DnsPacketParser.kt` is beautifully clean and entirely on-device. The key focus is that no third-party server is hardcoded. It works independently. I\'ve also noted a connection to `FirewallVpnService.kt`, which seems to be related.\n\n\n**Investigating DNS Configuration Options**\n\nI\'ve been examining the implications of `builder.addDnsServer(...)` within the `VpnService`. My goal is to allow users flexible control over their DNS resolution process. Now, I\'m thinking about user-selectable upstream DNS resolvers: System Default, Local Router, Cloudflare, Quad9, AdGuard, or even a custom IP. I\'m also considering local DNS sinkholing for blocked domains. This approach appears to align well with the requirement for local operation.\n\n\n**Confirming Upstream DNS Flexibility**\n\nI\'m solidifying the upstream DNS options. The system will handle NXDOMAIN on-device and forward allowed domains. I\'m focusing on user-selectable resolvers: System Default, Custom IP, Quad9, Cloudflare, and Google, ensuring no mandatory third-party server. This is fully local. I\'m starting to explore how to present this to the user.\n\n\n"
