  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Firewall Service**\n\nI\'ve been diving into `FirewallVpnService.kt`, specifically focusing on `buildNotification` and `onStartCommand`. I\'m starting to understand how the service is structured and how notifications are handled, which is crucial for the quick controls implementation the user requested. These seem like good places to begin implementing the user\'s requested controls.\n\n\n**Implementing Quick Controls**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the quick controls via a persistent notification within `FirewallVpnService`. I\'ve defined intent actions for various control options like start/stop, rule reloading, and quick network mode changes. The plan is to handle these actions in `onStartCommand` to make changes to VPN behavior. I\'ll need to figure out how to update the notification UI based on the VPN state.\n\n\n**Defining Action Handlers**\n\nI\'ve defined several intent actions and their corresponding handlers within the `FirewallVpnService`. Each action, such as reloading rules or applying quick block modes, now has a dedicated coroutine in `serviceScope`. I\'m starting to integrate these handlers and actions for managing network rules, switching firewall quick modes, and updating the VPN configuration. These actions call `reconfigureVpn()`, which is a key function to refresh the VPN settings.\n\n\n**Refining Notification Controls**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the quick control notification, defining actions such as \"Stop Firewall,\" \"Block Non-System,\" and network mode selections within `buildNotification()`. The `BigTextStyle` will display detailed status, including the active mode and network type, and instructions to use the quick controls. I\'ve also integrated receivers for device idle and screen events to update VPN settings accordingly. Specifically, I\'m handling `PowerManager.ACTION_DEVICE_IDLE_MODE_CHANGED` to reflect idle state changes.\n\n\n**Integrating Device Idle Checks**\n\nI\'m now integrating the device idle state into the firewall logic, ensuring it\'s checked on service start. I\'ve incorporated `PowerManager` to check `isDeviceIdleMode` and update the firewall accordingly. This information is passed into `establishVpn()` to be used during rule evaluation. I\'m also now dynamically configuring upstream DNS based on preferences for local functionality and to ensure no third-party server is hardcoded.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 378486516
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
