  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding New Dependencies**\n\nI\'ve just added some new dependencies to `FirewallVpnService.kt`, including imports for `PowerManager` and `UpstreamDnsType`. I\'m also adding a device idle broadcast receiver within `onCreate`. The intent filter will be applied when actions are performed.\n\n\n**Implementing Device State Logic**\n\nI\'m now incorporating logic within `onCreate` to register a `BroadcastReceiver` that will listen for screen on/off events, and device idle mode changes. I\'m also adding initial state checks, getting the `PowerManager` to assess if the device is currently in idle mode, so that I can set the initial state via `firewallManager.setDeviceIdleState`. I\'ve also defined the various actions that will be performed in the companion object.\n\n\n**Adding Quick Controls**\n\nI\'m currently focused on incorporating quick control action buttons into the notification. I\'ve defined actions for stopping the VPN, blocking non-system apps, toggling Wi-Fi only mode (or Normal mode depending on the current mode), and allowing all traffic. I am also adding descriptive text to the notification to explain how these controls work. Finally, I\'m setting the `isDeviceIdle` state to evaluate `ruleEngine`.\n\n\n"
