    thinking: "**Constructing Background Activity Section**\n\nI\'m now diving into `AppsScreen.kt` to craft the \"Background Activity\" section for NetGuardian. My focus is on providing users a granular control over background activity for individual applications. I\'m thinking of incorporating toggle options.\n\n\n**Analyzing Implementation Details**\n\nI\'ve moved on to meticulously analyzing how I\'ll implement background activity controls within `AppsScreen.kt`. I\'ve outlined a tabbed structure, with one tab for \"App Network Rules\" and the other for \"Background Activity,\" incorporating appropriate icons. The critical aspect is the \"Android & Manufacturer Limitations Card\" within the \"Background Activity\" tab. I\'m focusing on making this card expandable to explain Android OS version-based limitations. For example, older versions allow unrestricted sockets unless blocked by NetGuardian, while newer versions, like Oreo and Pie, introduce background execution limits and App Standby Buckets.\n\n\n**Detailing OS Restrictions**\n\nI\'m now detailing restrictions in Android versions 12, 13, and 14, focusing on the Phantom Process Killer and limits on foreground services and alarm scheduling. I\'m also examining the challenges presented by manufacturer battery managers like Samsung\'s \"Sleeping apps,\" Xiaomi\'s battery saver, Huawei\'s \"PowerGenie,\" and OnePlus\' \"Deep Optimization.\" These implementations terminate background processes and sockets, and I\'ll outline how NetGuardian needs to handle these OEM implementations to correctly provide the needed function to the user. I\'ll need to clearly explain these differences in the user interface.\n\n\n**Defining Network Behavior**\n\nI\'m now outlining how NetGuardian circumvents process-killing limitations, relying on the Linux IP networking layer via `VpnService`. I\'ve detailed how configuring network rules, like \"Block Background Network,\" instantly drops socket attempts under specified conditions. Furthermore, I am considering global quick actions such as \"Block All Background (Non-System)\" and a search bar to simplify the user experience, along with per-application activity cards that detail current background status.\n\n\n"
