  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Tab Navigation**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started implementing the tab navigation in `AppsScreen.kt`. I\'ve added a `selectedTab` state using `remember` and `mutableStateOf`. Currently, it\'s initialized to 0. Next, I\'m integrating the `TabRow` composable and configuring its `selectedTabIndex` to reflect the `selectedTab` state. I\'m focusing on getting the initial tab structure in place before fleshing out the tab content.\n\n\n**Refining Tab Content**\n\nI\'m now populating the tab content based on the `selectedTab` state. For the \"App Rules\" tab (index 0), I\'m integrating the existing list with search, filter chips, and batch actions. For \"Background Activity\" (index 1), I\'m displaying the search bar and the \"Android & Manufacturer Background Execution Limitations\" card. I\'ve got the tab titles and icons wired up and the content switching smoothly. Next is fine-tuning the data display within each tab.\n\n\n**Analyzing Android Limits**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the varying Android background restrictions across versions and OEMs. I\'m noting specific limits in Android 7.0 (Data Saver), 8.0/9.0 (Background Execution Limits), and 12+ (Phantom Process Killer). I\'m also breaking down OEM killer behaviors like Samsung\'s Sleeping Apps, Xiaomi\'s aggressive memory management, Huawei\'s PowerGenie, and OnePlus/Oppo\'s deep optimization. Furthermore, I\'ve clarified how NetGuardian achieves non-root background data control via `VpnService` packet sinkholing.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 168204887
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
