    thinking: "**Investigating Broken Layout**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the \"0 patterns layout broken\" issue. The primary question is why the app is displaying zero patterns. My line of investigation has led me to `AppDatabase.kt`, which seems like a potential source of the problem. I\'ll need to examine the `DatabaseCallback` and its `onCreate` method.\n\n\n**Analyzing Database Creation**\n\nI\'ve realized the `onCreate` method in `AppDatabase.kt` is only executed during the initial database creation or destructive migrations, not on subsequent app launches. The problem lies in the `populateDefaultBlocklists` function being bypassed if the database already existed. Consequently, the `blocklist` table remains empty, leading to the display of zero patterns due to zero sizes for ad, tracker, and malware domains. This explains the \"0 patterns\" issue.\n\n\n**Addressing Layout Overlap**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a layout issue: longer titles, like \"Malware & Phishing Protection,\" combined with the pattern count, cause wrapping or truncation. I\'m focusing on the `Row` layout and how the text elements interact with the switch. This leads to the \"0 patterns\" being in a broken position. To solve it, I intend to fix the data by populating the blocklist table with more realistic rules in the `MainViewModel.kt` `init` block (or `AppRepository` / `AppDatabase`), and I\'ll improve the text in `populateDefaultBlocklists`.\n\n\n**Refining Category Display**\n\nMy current focus is on enhancing the `CategoryCard` design, specifically addressing the cut-off text issue. I\'m shortening category titles and descriptions for better readability and a cleaner layout. For instance, I\'m proposing \"Ad Networks\" instead of \"Ad Blocking\" for the title. Moreover, I plan to improve the handling of zero domain counts and ensure a graceful display even if a category is empty.\n\n\n**Improving Card Layout**\n\nI\'m now investigating a more modern Material 3 layout for the `CategoryCard`. I\'m comparing the existing unweighted horizontal row with a cleaner design. The goal is to address the collision between the text and the switch, by introducing a `Card` that uses `Column` to allow for the use of vertical arrangement. This will enhance readability. I aim to improve the visual presentation and overall user experience.\n\n\n**Optimizing Card Design**\n\nI\'m now revisiting the `CategoryCard` layout, specifically focusing on its content. I am now replacing the `Row` with a `Column` to enhance vertical alignment. I\'m exploring an approach to integrate the icon, title, rule count, and the switch in a more aesthetically pleasing manner. The objective is to refine how elements are organized and displayed to enhance the overall usability.\n\n\n**Revising Card Aesthetics**\n\nI\'ve crafted an enhanced version of the `CategoryCard`. The updated design features a container for the icon, a concise title with ellipsis for overflow, and a pattern count on its dedicated line. I\'m dynamically displaying \"active patterns\" with a count greater than zero. Otherwise, I\'m displaying \"Built-in engine ready\" when the count is zero. The switch is appropriately spaced.\n\n\n**Evaluating Text Display**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the text layout in `PrivacyScreen.kt` within the \"DNS-Based Filtering\" card, specifically addressing potential truncation issues on narrower screens. I\'m noting the clean positioning of the description in my design, with no collision whatsoever. It spans the width properly, avoiding cramping or truncation from the switch.\n\n\n"
