    thinking: "**Refining Text Clarity**\n\nI\'ve been looking over the text lengths in `PrivacyScreen.kt`, specifically focusing on the Master DNS Card. I\'m streamlining the description for the \"Intercept and sinkhole known ad & tracker requests locally\" feature. My goal is \"Intercept and sinkhole ads & trackers locally on-device\", to improve brevity. Now I\'m considering modifications within the `Column` component.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Component Changes**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI tweaks. I\'m focusing on the component used to display \"DNS-Based Filtering\", I\'ve identified improvements for the `Column` layout within the `PrivacyScreen.kt` file. I plan to add a `Spacer` element to improve the spacing. Further refinements are on the horizon. I am also planning to review the \"Built-in Protection Rules\" card layouts for the `Category` cards.\n\n\n**Evaluating Category Display**\n\nI\'m now examining the `CategoryCard` composable, specifically the \"Malware & Phishing\" card. The aim is to ensure its title, description, and domain count accurately reflect its purpose and status. I\'m checking that the icon is visually appropriate and the toggle functionality operates as intended.\n\n\n**Assessing Row Composition**\n\nI am now focusing on the `Row` within the `CategoryCard` composable, seeking to improve its internal layout and spacing. I\'m taking a close look at how the `Modifier.weight` is applied to each of the contained `Row` components. I\'m focusing on ensuring its horizontal arrangement and vertical alignment, especially for the icons and text, are consistent. I am now evaluating the use of `Surface` and the spacing provided by `Arrangement.spacedBy`.\n\n\n**Optimizing Visual Presentation**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the layout within the `CategoryCard` composable. I\'m taking a close look at the arrangement of the title, badge, and switch elements to ensure they\'re visually appealing. I see the importance of ensuring the screen is always wide enough for each element, so there is no collision. I am especially focusing on the use of `Surface` to create a new row for the badge and the `maxLines` attribute for the title. I am now evaluating the color usage based on `domainCount`.\n\n\n**Refining Title and Subtitle**\n\nI\'m presently revising the text within the `Upstream DNS Resolver` card in `PrivacyScreen.kt`. I\'m streamlining the title to \"Upstream DNS Resolver\". I\'m also shortening the subtitle to \"Zero third-party tracking required. Route to your local gateway, offline loopback, or custom Pi-hole.\" I am also refining the radio option text within the same section.\n\n\n**Enhancing DNS Option Layout**\n\nI\'m now revising the layout of the `RadioButton` options within the upstream DNS resolver settings. I\'m focusing on improved visual clarity and readability. Specifically, I\'m integrating padding to provide a well-spaced UI. I\'ve also incorporated `lineHeight = 15.sp` and padding to prevent multi-line descriptions from clipping.\n\n\n**Adjusting TextField Behavior**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the interaction of the `OutlinedTextField` and the `Button` used for custom blocklist domain entry. I\'m focusing on the behavior associated with adding a new domain. I\'m taking a close look at the text field reset logic after a domain is added. I am now evaluating the visual feedback for the user after the button is clicked.\n\n\n\n**Reviewing Custom Domain**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `CustomDomainItem` composable, examining how individual custom domains are displayed. I\'m focusing on the visual styling of each domain entry, specifically the use of `Card`, `Row`, and `Text` components. I am evaluating how the `Switch` and `Icon` elements contribute to its functionality. I\'m also considering the layout and alignment of domain names, ensuring they are properly truncated.\n\n\n"
