  planner_response {
    response: "I have resolved the text cutoff and redesigned the **Built-in Protection Rules** and Privacy screen layout:\n\n- **Built-in Protection Rules Redesign**:\n  - Re-architected `CategoryCard` with a clean two-tiered layout: the top row houses the category icon, title, rule count badge, and the toggle switch with ample spacing, while the description spans full width underneath with generous line-height.\n  - Placed the pattern count inside a dedicated pill-style badge container right below the title so it never collides with or wraps under the switch.\n  - Added a graceful fallback state (`\"Active (built-in)\"`) so that if pattern counts are pending or unpopulated, the layout remains balanced and clean instead of showing a broken \"0 patterns\" label.\n  - Ensured the local database default blocklist rules (ads, trackers, and malware signatures) are pre-populated automatically on app startup.\n\n- **Shortened & Scannable Text Labels**:\n  - **Category Titles & Descriptions**: Shortened titles to **Ad Networks**, **Trackers & Analytics**, and **Malware & Phishing** with concise, high-contrast descriptions that fit comfortably across all screen widths.\n  - **Master DNS Card**: Refined \"DNS-Based Filtering\" to **DNS Filtering** with a clear, two-line capped explanation and protected switch padding.\n  - **Upstream DNS Resolver**: Compacted header text and adjusted radio item padding to prevent text from crowding or clipping.\n  - **Custom Domain Rules**: Added single-line truncation with ellipsis for custom domains so long URLs never push delete actions off-screen.\n  - **Quick Mode & Background Chips**: Weighted buttons and chips evenly across the screen with concise labels to ensure clean horizontal alignment on narrower displays."
    modified_response: "I have resolved the text cutoff and redesigned the **Built-in Protection Rules** and Privacy screen layout:\n\n- **Built-in Protection Rules Redesign**:\n  - Re-architected `CategoryCard` with a clean two-tiered layout: the top row houses the category icon, title, rule count badge, and the toggle switch with ample spacing, while the description spans full width underneath with generous line-height.\n  - Placed the pattern count inside a dedicated pill-style badge container right below the title so it never collides with or wraps under the switch.\n  - Added a graceful fallback state (`\"Active (built-in)\"`) so that if pattern counts are pending or unpopulated, the layout remains balanced and clean instead of showing a broken \"0 patterns\" label.\n  - Ensured the local database default blocklist rules (ads, trackers, and malware signatures) are pre-populated automatically on app startup.\n\n- **Shortened & Scannable Text Labels**:\n  - **Category Titles & Descriptions**: Shortened titles to **Ad Networks**, **Trackers & Analytics**, and **Malware & Phishing** with concise, high-contrast descriptions that fit comfortably across all screen widths.\n  - **Master DNS Card**: Refined \"DNS-Based Filtering\" to **DNS Filtering** with a clear, two-line capped explanation and protected switch padding.\n  - **Upstream DNS Resolver**: Compacted header text and adjusted radio item padding to prevent text from crowding or clipping.\n  - **Custom Domain Rules**: Added single-line truncation with ellipsis for custom domains so long URLs never push delete actions off-screen.\n  - **Quick Mode & Background Chips**: Weighted buttons and chips evenly across the screen with concise labels to ensure clean horizontal alignment on narrower displays."
