  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Launch Sequence**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining a foolproof, professional first-launch onboarding sequence and permission setup for NetGuardian, ensuring it aligns perfectly with the Android security model. I\'m carefully reviewing the requirements, starting with the need for a guided 10-step onboarding process. The goal is to make the entire process user friendly.\n\n\n**Crafting the User Onboarding**\n\nI\'m currently working on crafting the user onboarding wizard. I\'ve designed the first five screens: a welcome screen with no immediate permissions, an app explanation, a privacy promise outlining the local processing, and a setup checklist. Now I\'m focusing on the VPN permission screen, explaining that Android requires this permission for local firewall functionality. It\'s becoming clearer how to design for ease of use.\n\n\n**Refining the Onboarding Steps**\n\nI\'m now refining the final steps of the onboarding sequence. Screen six will handle notification permissions on Android 13 and later, clarifying the foreground service notification. Screen seven focuses on battery optimization, with options for users to grant unrestricted access or defer the setting. Screen eight presents optional privacy features. Screen nine provides a system access check.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Setup Flow**\n\nI\'m finalizing Screen 10, the \"Setup Complete\" screen, including a protection summary and \"Open Firewall\" button. I\'m also designing the \"Protection Setup\" page in Settings, displaying real-time permission states (VPN, Notifications, Battery Optimization, etc.) with [Fix] buttons. I\'m adding a \"Start Firewall?\" dialog to confirm startup and clarify local processing. The safe default is \"Allow all apps\".\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 815299024
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
