    thinking: "**Defining Diagnostic Model**\n\nI\'ve started building the structure for the `SystemAccessDiagnostics.kt` file. I\'m focusing on defining the data model within. I\'ve begun with an `enum` for `DiagnosticStatus` to represent the core states. I plan to use it in `data/` or `firewall/` or `ui/setup/`.\n\n\n**Constructing Diagnostic Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `SystemDiagnosticItem` data class with an enum for `DiagnosticStatus`. I\'ve added a diagnostic inspector that examines VPN authorization, firewall service, and notification permissions. I\'ve begun crafting the logic for determining their respective statuses, incorporating specific checks for VPN preparation and firewall service activity, and including different logic based on the Android API version for notification permissions.\n\n\n**Evaluating System Checks**\n\nI\'ve recently expanded the diagnostic checks to include foreground notification permissions and background operation restrictions using `PowerManager`. I\'m also now verifying app visibility by querying installed packages. Furthermore, I\'ve implemented database and network connectivity checks. Each check yields either a `READY` or `NEEDS_ATTENTION` status.\n\n\n"
