  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Onboarding Structure**\n\nI\'m now structuring the Onboarding Flow component, starting with `OnboardingWizardScreen.kt`. I\'m meticulously reviewing the specifications for each of the 10 screens that are needed for this flow. Screen 1, the welcome screen, already has a defined title: \"Take control.\"\n\n\n**Outlining Welcome Screen Details**\n\nI\'ve finalized the welcome screen details. It starts with a title \"Take control of your internet\" and a subtitle clarifying app functions. I\'m working on the design for a security/firewall illustration and the primary \"Get Started\" button. The secondary \"Learn how it works\" option advances to screen 2. No permissions are requested on this screen.\n\n\n**Detailing Permission Screens**\n\nI\'m now detailing Screens 4 and 5 in the onboarding flow. Screen 4 will be a setup checklist, clearly delineating required and optional items. The list includes Firewall VPN, Notifications, Background operation, and Privacy filters. I plan to use a progress indicator like \"X of 3 required steps complete.\" Screen 5, titled \"Firewall access,\" explains the VPN permission requirement, emphasizing local traffic filtering. The \"Allow VPN Access\" button triggers the `onRequestVpnPermission()` callback to obtain the necessary Android authorization.\n\n\n**Refining Permission Handling**\n\nI\'m now refining the handling of VPN and notification permissions. Specifically, I\'m integrating the post-dialog logic for Screen 5, including state updates for granted and denied VPN access. Next, I\'m implementing the conditional display for notification permissions (Screen 6), checking Android version and showing appropriate messaging for older versions. For Android 13+, the notification permission flow, success/failure states, and retry options are in progress. Finally, I\'ve started on the battery/background operation screen.\n\n\n**Implementing Battery Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing the battery optimization handling (Screen 7). I\'m using `powerManager.isIgnoringBatteryOptimizations()` to accurately detect the app\'s real state, not assuming it. If unrestricted, I display a \"permitted\" message. If restricted, a warning appears with an \"Open Battery Settings\" button and a \"Not Now\" option. I\'m being careful to explain its optionality and the manufacturer-specific nature of this setting.\n\n**Adding Privacy Enhancements**\n\nI\'m starting screen 8, \"Strengthen your privacy.\" I\'m including switches for tracker, ad, and malware domain blocking, plus custom DNS/blocklists. I\'m making it clear these features are optional enhancements, not core firewall requirements. This screen directly interacts with the `MainViewModel` and `PreferencesRepository`.\n\n**Finalizing System Checks**\n\nI\'m now on Screen 9, \"Checking your setup.\" I\'m implementing dynamic real-time checks for firewall (VPN authorization, service availability), notifications, battery optimization, app visibility (via installed application query), and storage. These checks will be run to complete the system check.\n\n\n"
