  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Tile Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the user\'s requirements for a professional Android Quick Settings Tile system and a persistent firewall notification within NetGuardian. I\'m prioritizing the implementation of real Android `TileService` implementations. The user\'s preferences are at the forefront of my mind.\n\n\n**Defining Tile States**\n\nI\'ve fleshed out the state definitions for the Quick Settings Tiles. I\'m focusing on \"Firewall,\" \"Block All Apps,\" \"Wi-Fi Only,\" and \"Mobile Data\" tiles. The \"Firewall\" tile will toggle VPN authorization, with strict state management reflecting actual service status. I\'m also ensuring meaningful labels and icons for each tile.\n\n\n**Implementing Notification System**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the persistent notification system. My focus is on robust foreground service management for firewall operation. I\'ve designed dynamic content updates for blocked apps and connections, and action buttons for \"Stop Firewall,\" \"Open App,\" and pause options. I am also planning for various notification states to cover scenarios like firewall activity, unexpected disconnection, and errors, ensuring clear and actionable user feedback. I\'m also planning the correct notification channels.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 905107459
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
