  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Firewall State**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing `FirewallStateRepository.kt`. I\'ve started by defining the `FirewallState` enum, identifying two key states: `STOPPED` (firewall not running) and `STARTING` (VPN service initialization in progress). I plan to expand this list as I analyze the necessary state transitions.\n\n\n**Expanding Firewall States**\n\nI\'ve expanded the `FirewallState` enum to include `RUNNING`, `PAUSED`, `ERROR`, and `VPN_PERMISSION_REQUIRED`, covering the full lifecycle. I also defined a `FirewallSnapshot` data class to capture the firewall\'s complete state, including network information and statistics, and implemented methods on the `FirewallStateRepository`. I\'m now thinking about the internal logic of how to store and manage this data.\n\n\n**Implementing Notifications**\n\nI\'m now designing `FirewallNotificationManager`, focusing on channel initialization. I\'ll create \"NetGuardian Protection\" (low importance) and \"NetGuardian Status\" channels. The goal is clear notifications, avoiding intrusive sounds for the protection channel. The manager will keep the user informed about the firewall\'s state through status notifications.\n\n\n**Designing Notifications**\n\nI\'m now detailing notification specifics. I\'ll include a \"NetGuardian Alerts\" channel for crucial alerts, with a popup. The foreground notification will display status, with distinct content based on running/paused states. For the running state, it will show blocked apps/connections, and for paused states, the remaining time before automatic resume. It\'ll have actions for stopping, pausing, resuming, and opening the app.\n\n\n**Refining Notification Content**\n\nI\'m finalizing the notification content. I\'ve defined `VISIBILITY_PRIVATE` for the main notification, providing a public version with title \"NetGuardian is active\" and text \"Device network protection enabled\". I\'m also planning an \"Unexpected Disconnect\" notification in the alert channel with title \"Firewall protection stopped\" offering \"Restore Protection\" and \"Open App\" actions. I will also make an error notification, with a title \"Firewall needs attention\". Finally, I\'ve designed a boot alert with the title \"Protection needs to be restored\".\n\n\n**Managing Pause State**\n\nI\'m now determining pause timer management. It seems logical to handle this within `FirewallVpnService`. When the pause action is initiated, I\'ll set the firewall state to `PAUSED` with an expiry timestamp and use a coroutine for automatic resume. I need to update the notification and quick settings tile with pause status, including remaining time, then when the timer elapses, the state returns to `RUNNING`.\n\n\n**Implementing Quick Mode**\n\nI\'m now implementing the quick mode feature for blocking non-system apps. I\'ve updated `FirewallStateRepository` and `FirewallDao` to set `isBlockAllActive = true` and `setBlockAllNonSystem(true)`. To preserve user rules, I\'m considering using either a backup snapshot or a flag in `PreferencesRepository` or `AppDatabase`. When exiting strict mode, I\'ll reset the non-system blocked rules or restore the previous state. Disabling will involve restoring the previous firewall policy, setting `QuickMode.NORMAL`, and reloading VPN rules.\n\nI\'m now also looking into a Wi-Fi only mode tile:\n- Label: \"Wi-Fi Only\".\n- Behavior: Wi-Fi traffic permitted, mobile data blocked.\n- Check hardware transport support: Display tile as `STATE_UNAVAILABLE` on devices without cellular radio.\n- When active: `QuickMode.WIFI_ONLY`\n- When inactive\n\n\n**Defining Tile Interaction**\n\nI\'m now detailing quick settings tile behavior and considering navigation. I\'ve designed a mobile data tile, differentiating it from the system switch, which will toggle per-app rules. I\'ll pass an intent action on long press to launch activities such as the \"dashboard\", \"apps\", or \"settings\" screens. I also considered Android 13+ APIs for requesting tile addition.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 566177455
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
