  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the New Tile**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of a \"Wi-Fi Only\" tile service, starting with the `WifiOnlyTileService.kt` file. I\'m focusing on the behavior: restricting internet access for apps configured to use it when the tile is active. The label will be \"Wi-Fi Only.\" I think this is a pretty straightforward tile to implement.\n\n\n**Assessing Transport Filtering**\n\nI\'ve just added checks to determine transport type filtering capability. If telephony features are missing, the tile will be unavailable with an \"Unsupported\" subtitle. When filtering is supported, the active state will show \"Cellular Blocked,\" and inactive will show \"All Transports.\" Tapping the tile will toggle the Wi-Fi Only mode. I am now creating the `WifiOnlyTileService.kt` file.\n\n\n"
