  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Navigation Logic**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got a plan for handling navigation. The core idea is to intercept clicks on the persistent notification and Quick Settings tile. I\'m going to add `onNewIntent` and check for the `EXTRA_ROUTE` intent extra within `MainActivity.kt`. It should be straightforward to navigate to the correct destination this way!\n\n\n**Adding Firewall State Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating firewall state observation. I\'ve updated `MainViewModel` to expose a `StateFlow` of `FirewallSnapshot` from the `FirewallStateRepository`. This means I can now reflect firewall state changes in `MainActivity`. I\'ll use `collectAsStateWithLifecycle` to observe the snapshot\'s state, allowing for display of \"PROTECTION ACTIVE\", \"STARTING...\", \"PAUSED\", etc. in the UI.\n\n\n**Refining UI State**\n\nOkay, the UI state logic is being refined. I\'m focusing on displaying more nuanced firewall states. \"ATTENTION NEEDED\" will be shown in red when the firewall is in an `ERROR` state, while a \"PROTECTION OFF\" message in muted red or gray will be displayed when the firewall is `STOPPED`. I\'m starting to build out a more helpful error state.\n\n**Adding Tile Discovery Support**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the first-time tile experience, making the Quick Settings tiles more discoverable. I\'m implementing in-app guidance for adding tiles and explaining their functions. For Android 13 and later, I\'ll leverage `StatusBarManager.requestAddTileService` to prompt users to directly add the tile. The Kotlin is ready for the API check!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
