  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Element**\n\nI\'ve been examining the `HeroStatusCard` composable within `DashboardScreen.kt`, specifically focusing on how its background changes based on its active state. When inactive, it uses `warningContainer` from `netGuardian` if the status is paused, otherwise uses `primaryContainer` from `MaterialTheme.colorScheme`.\n\n\n**Reviewing Color Customization**\n\nI\'ve refined the color scheme logic within the `HeroStatusCard` composable. Specifically, the button colors and text colors are updated depending on active state. It now accounts for `isPaused`, `isActive`, and `isError` status. For an active state, the button color should be error to denote a distinct \"Stop Firewall\" action.\n\n\n**Refining Color Usage**\n\nI\'m now making final adjustments to color usage. For StatCards, I\'ve defined specific colors for the title, value, subtitle, and borders based on `MaterialTheme.colorScheme`. I\'ve also assigned color logic based on data type, and context, e.g. \"blocked\" stats uses specific colors from `netGuardian`, others leverage `MaterialTheme.colorScheme`. The goal is to provide visual hierarchy and improve the overall aesthetic.\n\n\n**Implementing Color Consistency**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring consistent color application across different components. The \"TILE & NOTIFICATION\" badge leverages `primaryContainer` and `onPrimaryContainer`. The master toggle card\'s appearance and the switch colors are now determined by the `isFirewallActive` state. FilterChips are being styled to complement the existing theme. This aims to create a cohesive and visually intuitive interface.\n\n\n**Defining Button Colors**\n\nI\'m now nailing down button color schemes. The \"Block Non-System\" button uses `netGuardian.blockedContainer` when active, otherwise `surface`. I also implemented the correct logic and color usage for the \"Allow All Apps\" button, using the `primaryContainer` with some transparency to maintain visual distinction. I\'ve also implemented the color logic for the RecentActivityPreviewCard.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 339543339
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
