    thinking: "**Refining Dashboard Design**\n\nI\'m currently focused on refining the Quick Settings banner within `DashboardScreen.kt`. Specifically, I\'m updating lines 164-420. The goal is to ensure a visual consistency, using a `BorderStroke` with an `outlineVariant` color. I\'m also implementing a `primaryContainer` background with a `CircleShape`, and a `primary` tint.\n\n\n**Reviewing Color Theming**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously reviewing the color theming for the `HeroStatusCard` in the UI. I\'m focusing on consistency and clarity, especially when handling different states like paused, active, and error. I\'ve defined `cardBg`, `iconBg`, title color, subtitle color, and button colors based on these states. The goal is to ensure visual cues are intuitive for the user.\n\n\n**Updating Tile Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m currently updating color assignments within `DashboardScreen.kt`, specifically focusing on lines 421-600, within the `StatTilesSection` and `StatCard` composables. I\'ve defined `valueColor` and `iconTint` for various status tiles, such as \"Blocked Today\" and \"Active Network,\" using `netGuardian` and `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` elements. Additionally, I\'ve standardized the title and subtitle colors in `StatCard` to `onSurfaceVariant` and updated borders. Lastly, I\'ve customized the color theming in `QuickControlsCard` for the badge, and the master toggle, including the switch appearance.\n\n\n**Adjusting UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing aesthetic updates to several UI elements. I\'ve configured the color scheme for network profile chips, filter chips (including selected and unselected states), and outlined buttons (for both Block Non-System and Allow All Apps actions) to enhance visual clarity and consistency, using various color properties from `MaterialTheme.colorScheme` and `netGuardian`. I\'ve also set up colors for the Info note tint.\n\n\n**Implementing Recent Activity Colors**\n\nI\'m now implementing color adjustments to the Recent Activity section. Specifically, I\'m updating `color` properties for various elements. I\'ve switched the text color to `onSurface`, and primary to `primary`, and defined an outline variant border. Additionally, I\'ve styled for empty state, dividers and icon containers with surface variant background and rounded corners. Blocked logs have tint and container colors via the netguardian or material theme, with container text also utilizing netguardian values. Transparency borders are applied.\n\n\n"
