    thinking: "**Analyzing Color Scheme Usage**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the color scheme implementation. It\'s becoming clear that the component design leverages the MaterialTheme\'s color scheme for text. I\'ve noted a consistent pattern: `SleekPrimaryText` and `SleekBodyText` are both tied to `onSurface`, and `SleekMutedText` uses `onBackground`. I\'m exploring the implications of this approach for flexibility and theming.\n\n\n**Exploring Color Assignments**\n\nI\'m now investigating color assignments in more detail, specifically how the `MaterialTheme` colors map to custom color names. I\'ve mapped `SleekPrimary` to `primary`, `SleekPrimaryContainer` to `primaryContainer`, and so on, down to `StatusWarningAmber` mapping to `netGuardian.warning`. I\'m starting to think about whether these can be defined as helper properties. I\'m looking at `OnboardingWizardScreen.kt`, it\'s a single file and contains several private composables - let\'s see what happens if we define or replace these. I think this can potentially be done with a composable property: I\'m examining defining a property such as `private val MaterialTheme.onboardingPrimary`.\n\n\n"
